  "source_maps": "maplibre-gl-5.24.0.js ends with a relative '//# sourceMappingURL=maplibre-gl.js.map' comment (its last line). The map is not vendored: a browser only requests it with developer tools open, and then gets a same-origin 404; no request leaves the site. The CSS contains only data: URIs (its http://www.w3.org/2000/svg strings are XML namespaces inside them) and the JS carries no absolute http(s) URL that is fetched at runtime — its literals are the maplibre.org homepage and licence link in the banner and an upstream issue link in a comment. Library bytes are upstream's, unmodified, so each sha256 can be recomputed against the source_url.",
  "font_subsets": "The story page's visible text lies within Google's 'latin' block (U+0000-00FF, U+2000-206F and a few others) except for the two marked letters of 'Ribāṭ' (U+0101, U+1E6D), which 'latin-ext' covers, and one rightwards arrow (U+2192), which no Google subset covers and which therefore falls through to the fallback font exactly as it did when served by Google. Hence latin and latin-ext are vendored for every family, style and weight; cyrillic, cyrillic-ext, greek and vietnamese are dropped. Google served one identical file for IBM Plex Sans 300, 400, 500 and 600 (same sha256), so those four @font-face declarations share one vendored file per subset.",
  "user_agent": "The CSS2 endpoint was fetched with a Chrome 128 user agent; without one Google returns TTF faces and no unicode-range."
